%SIXMD 1
# @?INIT - START AND RESPAWN SYSTEM SERVICES

## @?OPTIONS

## @?OPERANDS

## DESCRIPTION

INIT IS THE FIRST USER PROCESS.  IT READS /CONFIG/INITTAB, STARTS THE
CONFIGURED SERVICES, WAITS FOR CHILDREN, AND RESPAWNS ENTRIES MARKED FOR
RESPAWN.

INIT MUST RUN AS PROCESS 1.

## @?FILES

### @?/CONFIG/INITTAB
SYSTEM SERVICE TABLE READ AT STARTUP.

## @?EXIT STATUS

### @?1 - STARTUP FAILED
INIT EXITS ONLY WHEN IT CANNOT RUN AS PROCESS 1 OR CANNOT LOAD ITS REQUIRED
STARTUP CONFIGURATION.
